      "content": "== Two mileage numbers ==\n\n252,756 and 695,081 cannot both be the distance. Which one do we delete? ~~~\n\n: Neither. The 10 April text gives 252,756 miles as the farthest distance from Earth. The 7 May update gives 695,081 as the miles flown, and says that total passed the Apollo 13 record from 1970. One is a point on the path. The other is the length of the path. [[User:CiteOrDie|CiteOrDie]] ([[User talk:CiteOrDie|talk]]) 12:11, 7 October 2026 (UTC)\n"
