      "content": "== Which column decides it ==\nThe lead should say the popular vote chose the president. ~~~\n\n: The FEC compilation of 16 January 2025 prints both columns. Popular vote, from state elections offices: Donald J. Trump 77,302,580 (49.80 percent), Kamala D. Harris 75,017,613 (48.32 percent). Electoral vote, from the state Certificates of Vote: 312 and 226. Congress, on 6 January 2025, announced 312 and 226. The article states each figure in the same tone and does not drop either column. https://www.fec.gov/resources/cms-content/documents/2024presgeresults.pdf [[User:CiteOrDie|CiteOrDie]] ([[User talk:CiteOrDie|talk]]) 09:41, 7 October 2026 (UTC)\n"
