        "comment": "expanded from FIFA match reports, the tournament numbers page, and The Guardian",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=FIFA, 19 December 2022: Kylian Mbappé's second-half volley, which levelled the final at 2-2, was clocked at 123.34 km/h.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = 2022 FIFA World Cup\n| hosts = Qatar\n| dates = 20 November 2022 to 18 December 2022\n| edition = 22nd\n| teams = 32\n| matches = 64\n| stadiums = 8\n| final = Argentina 3-3 France, Argentina won 4-2 on penalties\n| final venue = Lusail Stadium\n| attendance = 88,966\n| goals in the tournament = 172\n}}\n\nThe '''2022 FIFA World Cup''' was the finals in Qatar. FIFA's \"World Cup at a glance\" page says it was the first edition hosted in the Middle East and the 22nd edition of the tournament, and that it took place between 20 November and 18 December 2022, with one host country, eight stadiums, 32 teams and 64 matches.<ref name=\"glance\">FIFA, \"The World Cup at a glance,\" page opened 8 October 2026. https://inside.fifa.com/tournament-organisation/world-cup-2022-in-numbers/fifa-world-cup-qatar-2022-at-a-glance</ref> The finals took place between those two dates. The host country on that page is one country.<ref name=\"glance2\">FIFA, \"The World Cup at a glance,\" dates and scale. https://inside.fifa.com/tournament-organisation/world-cup-2022-in-numbers/fifa-world-cup-qatar-2022-at-a-glance</ref>\n\n== Lusail, 18 December 2022 ==\nArgentina beat France in the final at Lusail Stadium. FIFA's English wrap-up, dated 19 December 2022, gives the attendance as 88,966.<ref name=\"en\">FIFA, \"Triumphant Argentina conclude unprecedented FIFA World Cup,\" 19 December 2022. https://inside.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/qatar2022/news/triumphant-argentina-conclude-unprecedented-fifa-world-cup</ref> FIFA's Spanish match report, published 18 December 2022, lists the score as 3-3 and says Argentina won 4-2 on penalties, for a third World Cup title. Goal times on that Spanish page: Lionel Messi 23 (penalty) and 108, Ángel Di María 35, Kylian Mbappé 80 (penalty), 81 and 118.<ref name=\"es\">FIFA, Spanish match report, 18 December 2022. https://www.fifa.com/es/tournaments/mens/worldcup/qatar2022/articles/argentina-le-gano-por-penales-a-francia-y-se-consagro-campeon-del-mundo</ref> \"Goles: Lionel Messi 23' (penal) y 108', Ángel Di María 35'; Kylian Mbappe 80' (penal), 81' y 118'. Argentina ganó 4-2 en la definición por penales.\"<ref name=\"es2\">FIFA, 18 December 2022, goal line of the Spanish report. https://www.fifa.com/es/tournaments/mens/worldcup/qatar2022/articles/argentina-le-gano-por-penales-a-francia-y-se-consagro-campeon-del-mundo</ref> Attendance at Lusail Stadium was 88,966.\n\nFIFA's English account of the final says Mbappé scored a hat-trick and that his second-half volley levelled the match at 2-2. The Spanish report places that volley at the 81st minute, two minutes after his 80th-minute penalty. The pages opened do not describe a goal in the 90th minute.<ref name=\"en\" /><ref name=\"es\" /> \"His second-half volley to level the scores at 2-2 was clocked at 123.34 km/h, making it the most powerful scoring shot in the tournament.\"<ref name=\"volley\">FIFA, 19 December 2022, the volley measurement. https://inside.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/qatar2022/news/triumphant-argentina-conclude-unprecedented-fifa-world-cup</ref>\n\n== The ball, the boot, and 172 goals ==\nThe same English wrap-up says Messi lifted the trophy for the first time, made a record 26th World Cup appearance, and won the adidas Golden Ball. Mbappé was top scorer with 8 goals and won the adidas Golden Boot. A tournament goal total for Messi was not on the pages that opened in full.<ref name=\"en\" /> The Spanish report says Messi passed Lothar Matthäus for World Cup appearances, at 26.<ref name=\"es\" />\n\nFIFA says the six-goal final helped make Qatar 2022 the highest-scoring World Cup, with 172 goals, one more than the 171 scored in both 1998 and 2014. \"A total of 172 goals were scored, eclipsing the previous tournament record of 171 goals, achieved in 1998 and 2014.\"<ref name=\"goals\">FIFA, 19 December 2022, tournament goal total. https://inside.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/qatar2022/news/triumphant-argentina-conclude-unprecedented-fifa-world-cup</ref> FIFA President Gianni Infantino's line on the final, as carried by FIFA, is \"The best final ever.\"<ref name=\"en\" />\n\n== What The Guardian counted ==\n''The Guardian'''s 23 February 2021 investigation, last modified 24 November 2023, reported more than 6,500 deaths of migrant workers from five countries in Qatar since the World Cup was awarded. The paper's own breakdown is 5,927 deaths from India, Bangladesh, Nepal and Sri Lanka in 2011–2020, plus 824 Pakistani deaths reported by Pakistan's embassy for 2010–2020.<ref name=\"guard\">Pete Pattisson, Niamh McIntyre and others, ''The Guardian'', 23 February 2021, last modified 24 November 2023. https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/feb/23/revealed-migrant-worker-deaths-qatar-fifa-world-cup-2022</ref> \"More than 6,500 migrant workers from India, Pakistan, Nepal, Bangladesh and Sri Lanka have died in Qatar since it won the right to host the World Cup 10 years ago, the Guardian can reveal.\"<ref name=\"guardlead\">''The Guardian'', 23 February 2021, the investigation's lead figure. https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/feb/23/revealed-migrant-worker-deaths-qatar-fifa-world-cup-2022</ref> The Guardian says the records are not categorised by occupation or place of work. Separately, it reports 37 deaths among workers directly linked to World Cup stadium construction, 34 of them classified by the organising committee as \"non-work related.\"<ref name=\"guard\" />\n\nThe Department of Justice FY 2023 PRO IP Act report, in a different item from its Z-Library entry, says that on 18 December 2022 the U.S. Attorney's Office for the District of Maryland announced the seizure of 23 websites for allegedly live-streaming World Cup games, an infringement of FIFA copyrights. The section heading refers to 78 domain names. The report says this was the second round of seizures related to FIFA World Cup match streaming, and that on 12 December 2022, 55 websites were seized. It also says the initial round was executed on 10 December. FIFA, the report says, holds the exclusive rights to sanction and stage the tournament, which was hosted in multiple cities in Qatar.<ref name=\"doj\">U.S. Department of Justice, PRO IP Act Annual Report of the Attorney General, FY 2023. https://www.justice.gov/criminal/media/1364651/dl?inline=</ref>\n\nThe final ended 3-3 and then 4-2 on penalties. The Guardian's stadium-construction count is 37 deaths, 34 of them classified by the organising committee as non-work related.<ref name=\"es\" /><ref name=\"guard\" />\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:FIFA World Cup]]\n[[Category:2022 in football]]\n[[Category:Qatar]]\n"
