        "daysAgo": 9,
        "comment": "expanded from Variety, the Netflix title page, and Rotten Tomatoes",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Rotten Tomatoes, page opened 8 October 2026: all eight episodes are marked aired on 3 October 2025.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Monster: The Ed Gein Story\n| network = Netflix\n| premiere = 3 October 2025\n| episodes = 8\n| rating = TV-MA\n| creators = Ryan Murphy and Ian Brennan\n| lead = Charlie Hunnam\n| tomatometer = 22 percent from 41 reviews\n}}\n\n'''Monster: The Ed Gein Story''' is a 2025 television season on Netflix. Variety said the third installment of Ryan Murphy and Ian Brennan's anthology would premiere worldwide on Netflix on 3 October 2025, with Charlie Hunnam as Ed Gein. Murphy and Brennan created the series and executive produce. Brennan is also the writer. Hunnam is an executive producer as well as the lead.<ref name=\"var\">Variety, 27 August 2025. https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/monster-the-ed-gein-story-netflix-release-date-first-look-1236499019/</ref> The Netflix title page, opened 8 October 2026, lists 2025, eight episodes, TV-MA, and drama, and names Charlie Hunnam, Laurie Metcalf, and Suzanna Son.<ref name=\"nf\">Netflix title page, opened 8 October 2026. https://www.netflix.com/title/81783093</ref>\n\nThe record here is the season: network, date, creators, credits, and the notices printed about it.\n\n== Who directed it ==\nVariety said Brennan directed two episodes and Max Winkler directed six. Other executive producers named in that piece are Max Winkler, Eric Kovtun, Scott Robertson, Nissa Diederich, Louise Shore, and Carl Franklin, along with Murphy, Brennan, and Hunnam.<ref name=\"var-dir\">Variety, directors and executive producers, 27 August 2025. https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/monster-the-ed-gein-story-netflix-release-date-first-look-1236499019/</ref> Two plus six is eight, which matches the episode count on the title page.<ref name=\"nf\" />\n\nThe creator line is not identical on every page. Variety says Murphy and Brennan created the series. The Netflix title page's creator credit is Ian Brennan.<ref name=\"var\" /><ref name=\"nf-creator\">Netflix title page, creator credit, opened 8 October 2026. https://www.netflix.com/title/81783093</ref> Brennan is credited as creator on the Netflix title page. Both sentences are printed. The article keeps both.\n\n== Episodes and names ==\nEpisode titles on the Netflix page run from \"Mother!\" through \"The Godfather.\" Runtimes on that page run from 45 minutes to 1 hour 5 minutes.<ref name=\"nf\" /> Rotten Tomatoes, opened 8 October 2026, marks all eight episodes as aired on 3 October 2025, the same day as the premiere.<ref name=\"rt\">Rotten Tomatoes, page opened 8 October 2026. https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/monster_2022/s03</ref> The eight episodes went up together.\n\nRotten Tomatoes lists the release date as 3 October 2025 and the rating as TV-MA. It names the creators as Ryan Murphy and Ian Brennan. Its role list includes Charlie Hunnam as Ed Gein, Laurie Metcalf as Augusta Gein, Tom Hollander as Alfred Hitchcock, and Suzanna Son as Adeline Watkins.<ref name=\"rt-cast\">Rotten Tomatoes, credits, page opened 8 October 2026. https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/monster_2022/s03</ref>\n\nVariety's additional cast, from the Netflix description it printed, is Tom Hollander, Laurie Metcalf, Suzanna Son, Vicky Krieps, Olivia Williams, Lesley Manville, Joey Pollari, Charlie Hall, Tyler Jacob Moore, Mimi Kennedy, Will Brill, Greyson K. Reilly, and Robin Weigert.<ref name=\"var-cast\">Variety, cast in the Netflix description, 27 August 2025. https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/monster-the-ed-gein-story-netflix-release-date-first-look-1236499019/</ref>\n\n== What the description says ==\nVariety printed Netflix's official description. It sets the season in 1950s rural Wisconsin and says Gein's story is tied to later Hollywood horror, naming ''Psycho'', ''The Texas Chain Saw Massacre'', and ''The Silence of the Lambs''. The sentence Variety quotes begins, \"In the frozen fields of 1950s rural Wisconsin, a friendly, mild-mannered recluse named Eddie Gein lived quietly on a decaying farm.\"<ref name=\"var-log\">Variety, Netflix official description, 27 August 2025. https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/monster-the-ed-gein-story-netflix-release-date-first-look-1236499019/</ref> That is the description the release printed.\n\n== The scores and the tag ==\nRotten Tomatoes, opened 8 October 2026, showed a 22 percent Tomatometer from 41 reviews and a 49 percent Popcornmeter from 1,000 or more ratings.<ref name=\"rt\" /> A Globe and Mail review quoted on that page, dated 22 October 2025, and written by Amber Dowling, says: \"For all its craft and conviction, this series doesn't illuminate our fascination with evil so much as indulge it, and that's the real horror.\"<ref name=\"rt-rev\">Rotten Tomatoes, quoting Amber Dowling, Globe and Mail, 22 October 2025; page opened 8 October 2026. https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/monster_2022/s03</ref>\n\nNetflix's own \"This show is …\" labels on the title page include \"Golden Globe Nominee,\" along with anthology, 1950s, and true crime. That nominee line is a platform tag. It is not a separate awards-body citation.<ref name=\"nf-tag\">Netflix title page, \"This show is …\" labels, opened 8 October 2026. https://www.netflix.com/title/81783093</ref>\n\nThe record used here is the premiere date, the episode count, the credits, the scores, and the tag, each pinned to the page that printed it.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Television series]]\n[[Category:2025 television]]\n"
