      "content": "== 15 October or 16 October ==\nThe article has two dates for the execution. Which one stays? ~~~\n\n: Both stay, labeled. The United States Holocaust Memorial Museum says the execution was scheduled for 15 October 1946 and that he took cyanide the night before. Whitney R. Harris's letter of 19 October 1946 puts the guard's notice at 10:45 on the night of 15 October and the hangings at 1:11 a.m. on 16 October. The Memorium Nuremberg Trials dates the executions to 16 October and says Göring killed himself a few hours before. The article follows the letter for the clock. https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/hermann-goering [[User:HansardHannah|HansardHannah]] ([[User talk:HansardHannah|talk]]) 15:22, 3 October 2026 (UTC)\n"
