        "user": "HansardHannah",
        "daysAgo": 10,
        "comment": "expanded from the Warner Bros. page, the home-entertainment release, and Deadline",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Warner Bros. Discovery Home Entertainment, 24 March 2026: running time 136 minutes; digital release 31 March 2026; 4K UHD, Blu-ray, and DVD on 5 May 2026.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Wuthering Heights\n| year = 2026\n| director = Emerald Fennell\n| screenplay = Emerald Fennell, from Emily Brontë\n| starring = Margot Robbie, Jacob Elordi\n| us release = 13 February 2026\n| international = beginning 11 February 2026\n| runtime = 136 minutes\n| rating = R\n| worldwide gross = over $230 million\n}}\n\n'''Wuthering Heights''' is a 2026 film written and directed by Emerald Fennell. As of pages opened on 8 October 2026, it was already out. Warner Bros. Pictures' site said it would be in theaters nationwide in the United States on 13 February 2026, and internationally beginning 11 February.<ref name=\"wb\">Warner Bros. Pictures, official site, page opened 8 October 2026. https://www.wutheringheightsfilm.com/</ref> Warner Bros. Discovery Home Entertainment later gave the running time as 136 minutes and the rating as R, for sexual content, some violent content, and language. The same notice said the film had earned over $230 million at the worldwide box office.<ref name=\"pr\">PR Newswire / Warner Bros. Discovery Home Entertainment, 24 March 2026. https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/wuthering-heights-302722697.html</ref>\n\nThe screenplay is by Fennell, based on Emily Brontë's novel. The home-entertainment copy calls the film a \"bold and original interpretation,\" and says Cathy and Heathcliff's forbidden passion \"turns from romantic to intoxicating in an epic tale of lust, love and madness.\"<ref name=\"pr-line\">PR Newswire / Warner Bros. Discovery Home Entertainment, studio logline, 24 March 2026. https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/wuthering-heights-302722697.html</ref> That is the distributor's sentence. The dates and the credits are plainer.\n\n== Dates ==\nThe Warner Bros. page separates the calendar by territory. International release begins 11 February 2026. The United States date is 13 February 2026.<ref name=\"wb\" /> Two months later, the home-entertainment notice set digital release for 31 March 2026, and 4K UHD, Blu-ray, and DVD for 5 May 2026.<ref name=\"pr-home\">PR Newswire / Warner Bros. Discovery Home Entertainment, home-video dates, 24 March 2026. https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/wuthering-heights-302722697.html</ref>\n\nDeadline, on 24 April 2026, reported an HBO Max premiere on Friday, 1 May 2026, and an HBO linear debut the next day at 8:00 p.m. ET. An American Sign Language version was also set to stream on HBO Max.<ref name=\"dl\">Deadline, 24 April 2026. https://deadline.com/2026/04/wuthering-heights-streaming-date-hbo-max-1236870956/</ref> The disc, the stream, and the linear broadcast are three different lines on two notices. The running time does not change with them. It stays 136 minutes.<ref name=\"pr\" />\n\n== Cast and companies ==\nThe Warner Bros. page stars Margot Robbie opposite Jacob Elordi, with Hong Chau, Shazad Latif, Alison Oliver, Martin Clunes, and Ewan Mitchell.<ref name=\"wb-cast\">Warner Bros. Pictures, cast and producers, page opened 8 October 2026. https://www.wutheringheightsfilm.com/</ref> The home-entertainment release says Robbie plays Cathy and Elordi plays Heathcliff.<ref name=\"pr\" />\n\nProducers are Josey McNamara, Fennell, and Robbie. Executive producers are Sara Desmond and Tom Ackerley. The film is presented by Warner Bros. Pictures and MRC. It is a Lie Still and LuckyChap Entertainment production.<ref name=\"wb\" /> The LuckyChap credit sits on the Warner Bros. page.\n\n== Crew ==\nThe same home-entertainment release credits original songs by Charli XCX, cinematography by Linus Sandgren, production design by Suzie Davies, editing by Victoria Boydell, and costumes by Jacqueline Durran. The score composer named there is Anthony Willis.<ref name=\"pr-crew\">PR Newswire / Warner Bros. Discovery Home Entertainment, credits, 24 March 2026. https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/wuthering-heights-302722697.html</ref> Fennell is the writer and the director on the Warner Bros. page, and the screenwriter again on the home-entertainment notice, which ties the script to Brontë's novel.<ref name=\"wb\" /><ref name=\"pr\" />\n\nThe box-office sentence on that notice is \"over $230 million,\" not a dollar-and-cents total. No finer figure was on the pages opened for this article.<ref name=\"pr\" />\n\n== After the theaters ==\nBy 24 March 2026 the film was being sold for home viewing, with the theatrical gross already stated as over $230 million.<ref name=\"pr-home\" /> By 24 April the streaming date was public: HBO Max on 1 May, HBO the next evening at 8:00 p.m. ET, and an American Sign Language version on the streaming service.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The page opened on 8 October 2026 treats the film as released.<ref name=\"wb\" />\n\nThe rating line is the board's, printed in full on the home-entertainment notice: R for sexual content, some violent content, and language.<ref name=\"pr\" />\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Films]]\n[[Category:2026 films]]\n"
