        "user": "CiteOrDie",
        "daysAgo": 8,
        "comment": "expanded from Variety, Netflix Tudum, and the Netflix title page",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Netflix Tudum, 15 September 2025, quoting Blanc: \"This was dressed as a miracle, it's just a murder. And I solve murders.\"}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Wake Up Dead Man\n| year = 2025\n| director = Rian Johnson\n| writer = Rian Johnson\n| series = third Benoit Blanc film\n| theatrical = 26 November 2025, select theaters, two weeks\n| netflix = 12 December 2025\n| rating = PG-13\n| premiere = Toronto, 6 September 2025\n}}\n\n'''Wake Up Dead Man''' is a 2025 film directed, written, and co-produced by Rian Johnson. Variety described it as the third Benoit Blanc film, and as \"the third and darkest chapter\" of Johnson's murder-mystery series. Select theaters were set for 26 November 2025, for a two-week run, and Netflix for 12 December 2025.<ref name=\"var\">Variety, 2 September 2025. https://variety.com/2025/film/news/wake-up-dead-man-knives-out-theatrical-release-netflix-1236504241/</ref> Netflix Tudum gave the same two dates, and added the festival calendar: a world premiere at the Toronto International Film Festival on 6 September, and the opening of the BFI London Film Festival on 8 October.<ref name=\"tudum\">Netflix Tudum, 15 September 2025. https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/wake-up-dead-man-is-beyond-belief</ref> The Netflix title page, opened 8 October 2026, lists the film as 2025, PG-13, and available to watch.<ref name=\"nf\">Netflix title page, opened 8 October 2026. https://www.netflix.com/title/81458424</ref>\n\n== The cast ==\nVariety's cast list is Daniel Craig, Josh O'Connor, Glenn Close, Josh Brolin, Mila Kunis, Jeremy Renner, Kerry Washington, Andrew Scott, Cailee Spaeny, Daryl McCormack, and Thomas Haden Church.<ref name=\"var-cast\">Variety, cast list, 2 September 2025. https://variety.com/2025/film/news/wake-up-dead-man-knives-out-theatrical-release-netflix-1236504241/</ref> The Netflix title page names Daniel Craig, Josh O'Connor, and Glenn Close at the top, and carries the wider cast through Daryl McCormack.<ref name=\"nf\" />\n\nIn the synopsis Variety printed, Benoit Blanc is Craig, the young priest Jud Duplenticy is O'Connor, Monsignor Jefferson Wicks is Brolin, and police chief Geraldine Scott is Kunis.<ref name=\"var\" />\n\n== The case on the page ==\nVariety's synopsis sends Blanc to investigate a seemingly impossible murder after Duplenticy is sent to assist Wicks. Scott joins the investigation.<ref name=\"var-syn\">Variety, official synopsis, 2 September 2025. https://variety.com/2025/film/news/wake-up-dead-man-knives-out-theatrical-release-netflix-1236504241/</ref> Tudum places the story in a small hamlet in upstate New York. A line Tudum attributes to Blanc says the case \"was dressed as a miracle\" and is \"just a murder,\" and then, \"And I solve murders.\"<ref name=\"tudum-line\">Netflix Tudum, Blanc line and setting, 15 September 2025. https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/wake-up-dead-man-is-beyond-belief</ref>\n\nThe synopsis stops there.\n\n== The chapel ==\nTudum says most of the drama unravels in a cavernous chapel built by production designer Rick Heinrichs. Johnson described the look as gothic. Cinematography is by Steve Yedlin. The score is by Nathan Johnson.<ref name=\"tudum-crew\">Netflix Tudum, design and music, 15 September 2025. https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/wake-up-dead-man-is-beyond-belief</ref> Yedlin shot the film and Nathan Johnson wrote the score.\n\nThe festival dates sit in front of the commercial dates. Toronto on 6 September, London on 8 October, select theaters on 26 November for two weeks, Netflix on 12 December.<ref name=\"var\" /><ref name=\"tudum\" /> By the title page opened on 8 October 2026, the film was listed as available.<ref name=\"nf\" /> Variety's billing sentence is longer than the title. It says Blanc \"returns for his most dangerous case yet in the third and darkest chapter of Rian Johnson's murder mystery opus.\" Tudum's 15 September 2025 article places the Toronto premiere on 6 September and the London opening on 8 October, then repeats the 26 November theatrical date and the 12 December Netflix date. The title page, opened the following October, calls the film a PG-13 drama and lists it as available to watch.<ref name=\"var\" /><ref name=\"tudum\" /><ref name=\"nf\" />\n\n== The title page ==\nThe title page's own line is short: 2025, PG-13, drama, and the cast from Craig through the names it displays.<ref name=\"nf-meta\">Netflix title page, rating and year, opened 8 October 2026. https://www.netflix.com/title/81458424</ref> Variety's adjective for the chapter, \"darkest,\" stays in Variety's sentence.<ref name=\"var\" /> The line the article treats as the useful one is Blanc's, because Tudum prints it as his: dressed as a miracle, just a murder.<ref name=\"tudum-line\" />\n\nJohnson is the director, the writer, and a producer. The release pattern is theatrical, then the stream, on the dates above.<ref name=\"var\" />\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Films]]\n[[Category:2025 films]]\n"
